## Appendix: Ant publication and interpretation corrections

The [kinematics follow-up](https://github.com/BurnyCoder/reinforcement-learning-locomotion-steering-vectors/blob/main/reports/fact-check-2026-10-29/kinematics-follow-up.md) fixes nondefault-window slope units, unavailable single-window trends, angular branch cuts and timestep validation. Published default-window mean summaries retain their recorded values within the documented tolerance. A finite observed heading offset does not establish bounded long-run behavior or cessation of turning.

The current Ant narrative, comparison tables and figures are generated from original JSON/NPZ artifacts by `uv run --locked --no-sync python scripts/build_ant_publication.py`. The input manifest pins Hub revision `{{source_revision}}` and every file's SHA256. The publication stage does not load policy weights or invoke a simulator. New derived summaries, including clipping prevalence and additional display intervals, are labelled descriptive; they do not change original hypotheses, selections, thresholds or decisions.

The original confirmation estimator averages available post-onset values within each episode, including the retained zero convention for a pre-onset ending. The later audit's headline uses a different bootstrap interval method on a separate cohort. Both must be named when comparing numbers. Evaluation-reward graphs show observed episode segments and their denominators, not fabricated training curves. Display-only trajectory downsampling retains onset and endpoints; statistics use full recorded arrays.

{{cohort_table}}

The new seed registry records both reservations and consumption. It prevents a new application from reusing the later audit resets while allowing explicit historical audit verification. Historical cache identities are not migrated. The exact research dependencies remain pinned for reproduction; newer tooling is limited to publication. Source/license uncertainties for Baukit and upstream weights remain disclosed in the [source audit](https://github.com/BurnyCoder/reinforcement-learning-locomotion-steering-vectors/blob/main/docs/sources.md).

The [completion ledger](https://github.com/BurnyCoder/reinforcement-learning-locomotion-steering-vectors/blob/main/docs/ant-publication.md) records checks, failures, retries, receipts, and requirements that remain historically unmet or inapplicable. The [interactive explorer]({{site}}) exposes positive, null and failed conditions from the same evidence.

## Independent saved-data verification, 2026-10-29

The [new claim ledger and correction report](https://github.com/BurnyCoder/reinforcement-learning-locomotion-steering-vectors/blob/main/reports/fact-check-2026-10-29/report.md) independently recomputes saved extraction, paired effects, gates, selection and later audit statistics without model execution. It qualifies ensemble ranks, optimality arguments, historical runtime checks and kinematic timing. Original observations and selections remain unchanged. E1 fitted-regression claims, neural response-axis derivation and media replay correspondence are historical evidence, not independently revalidated model behavior. Use `scripts/build_publication.py` for the complete saved-data rebuild.

